    <item>
      <title>The Lighthouse Keeper's Last Broadcast</title>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">sample-0106</guid>
      <itunes:subtitle>Forty years of weather logs, and one entry that shouldn't exist.</itunes:subtitle>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <p>On the final night before the light goes automated, the keeper reads out forty years of
        weather logs — and one entry that was never supposed to be recorded.</p>
        <p>We talk maritime superstition, the economics of solitude, and why a foghorn is basically a
        very sad synthesizer. Full sources on <a href="https://example.com/notes/0106">the show notes page</a>.</p>
      ]]></description>
